# ==============================================================================
# PostgreSQL password file template (.pgpass)
# ==============================================================================
# Copy this file to config/.pgpass/.pgpass, next to the checkout, and add real
# credentials.
#
# Format: hostname:port:database:username:password
#
# Examples:
#   db.example.com:5432:sead_production:sead_user:your_password_here
#   localhost:5432:*:postgres:admin123
#   *.example.com:5432:*:user:pass
#
# Wildcards (*) can be used for any field except the password.
#
# Security:
#   chmod 600 config/.pgpass/.pgpass
#   Never commit the real file.
#
# Documentation: https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/libpq-pgpass.html
# ==============================================================================

# Add database credentials here (one per line):
# hostname:port:database:username:password
